    "description": "CMK Corporation develops, produces, and markets various printed circuit boards in Japan, China, Southeast Asia, Europe, the United States, and internationally. The company offers automotive PCB; high heat dissipation or high current copper base and composite metal PCBs; semi-flex and rigid-flex PCB series; high frequency correspondence PCBs; high-multi-layer-PCB; PPBU series; through-hole PCBs; and double-sided multilayer PCBs. The company's products are used in automotive, medical, telecommunications, and aerospace industries. CMK Corporation has a strategic alliance with Guangdong Ellington Electronic Technology Co., Ltd. The company was formerly known as Chuo Meiban Kogyo Co., Ltd. and changed its name to CMK Corporation in 1984. CMK Corporation was founded in 1959 and is headquartered in Shinjuku, Japan."
